This independent implementation adapts methods and calculations from:
pBFSLab/rLNM — Robust Lesion Network Mapping
https://github.com/pBFSLab/rLNM
Pinned commit: 059ade5fc2a332bb2a246ef7db0bd7c4217446e4
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adapted components include mean FC row projection, percentile-based signed
overlap, spatial lesion translation and frequency-matching annealing,
leave-one-lesion-out shared regressors, OLS residuals, Welch statistics,
pooled-SD effects, and permutation/FDR calculations. Python I/O, configuration,
provenance, deterministic per-draw random streams, reports, and validation
infrastructure are new. Changes and departures are described in docs/methods.md.

Please cite the originating study when using these methods:
Cui W et al. Robust lesion network mapping reveals symptom-specific circuits.
bioRxiv. https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.05.18.725812

Upstream example data are downloaded separately, are not redistributed by this
repository, and retain their original attribution and terms. This repository
does not imply endorsement by the upstream authors or by BCBtoolkit/Lead-DBS.

